From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: linux-a9 <linux-a9@localhost>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 11:29:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/14] media: apple: vxd: add the H.264 (AVC) command-stream builder
 (R3c)

docs/periph/ds-vxd-cmdstream.md sections 1-15 turned out to describe the
kext's HEVC picture path (0xfffffff0062960a0 is reached for NAL types
0x20-0x22).  The AVC path is HOST_H264DecodeFrame 0xfffffff0062a15f0 ->
DecodePictureInternal 0x62a0c00 -> DecodeExecuteH264VLD 0x62c4c98 and is
decoded in section 16.3-16.6.  It speaks Imagination's DXVA control-
allocation format (the open dxva_fw_ctrl.h of Intel's psb_video), one
command chunk and one kind-1 packet (mailbox 0x81) per slice:

  CTRL_ALLOC_HEADER   0x90000000 + slice params, strides, first and
                      last MB, chroma format
  CMD_DMA             the 0x440-byte CAVLC table, type VLC
  REGVALPAIR          26 constant VLC table address registers
  SR_SETUP            {0xb0000001, header bits & 31, bytes}, RBDU
  BITSTREAM_DMA       the slice NAL from the OUTPUT buffer, whole header
                      words skipped by address
  REGVALPAIR          entropy front end: control, SPS0, PPS0, PIC0,
                      SLICE0, SLICE1, first MB
  RENDEC_BLOCKs       back end (same words + stored-MB buffer + long-term
                      mask), flat scaling lists, RefPicList0 as DPB slots,
                      reference Y/UV addresses, picture size, operating
                      mode, output Y/UV, intra buffer, weight
                      denominators, cache policy, stride, chroma format
  CMD_COMPLETION      0x60000000

The chunks follow each other with no pad and there is no per-picture
kind-4 chunk.  Apple's 0x6000/0x7000 register banks line up with the
public MSVDX VEC/CMDS offsets (FE_SPS0 0x200, BE_SPS0 0x2d8,
BE_BASE_ADDR_CUR_PIC 0x2ec, VLC_TABLE_ADDR0 0xec, luma/chroma recon base
0xc/0x10, intra buffer 0x18, ...).

Generate the 544-entry CAVLC table from Imagination/TI's GPL-2.0
h264_vlc_table_data, including the 4:2:2 chroma-DC entries. Its first
520 entries also match MIT psb_video's ui16H264VLCTableData.

New encoders: the populated CTRL_ALLOC_HEADER, the 0x5 RENDEC_BLOCK
(never merged), the 0xe DMA, and an unpadded chunk end.  The builder is
a pure function of SPS, PPS, DECODE_PARAMS, the parsed slices, their
RefPicList0 and the device addresses.  It refuses what the recipe does
not cover yet: interlace, 4:2:2/4:4:4, high bit depth, FMO, scaling
matrices, the 8x8 transform, weighted prediction and B/SP/SI slices.
CABAC follows the same recipe (entropy flag, cabac_init_idc, aligned
header) but is unvalidated.

Checked on the host: scripts/vdec/host-cmdstream.sh builds this file
against shims and diffs every picture of three test streams (I, P,
4-slice) word for word against tools/ds-video/cmdstream.py --gen, an
independent implementation of section 16.  All 7 pictures match.

Signed-off-by: linux-a9 <linux-a9@localhost>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <maintainer@example.invalid>


Provenance refresh: generate the unchanged 544-entry CAVLC table from
Imagination/TI GPL-2.0 source; include the pinned source and generator.
